  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdd `corner_blends_keep_named_solid_restarts_at_each_level` to the existing `adaptive_entry_pieces` test binary.\nOne Offset rings operation contains a large pocket and a separate tiny pocket.\nIt requests a helix and corner blends at Z -4 and -8 mm.\n\nThe test checks:\n- Added planar corner arcs at each level, compared with a sharp reference.\n- Finite chained motion and helix entries in the large pocket.\n- Unchanged solid plunge sites and depths.\n- A diagnostic with the XY site and Z level for every solid plunge.\n\nThis is missing coverage, not a production fix.\nThe new test passes on unchanged production code.\nNo production code, dependencies, process files, or extra test binaries change.\nThe decision record explains the fixture and alternatives.\n\n## Readings\n\nRead the full issue thread, `pocket_emit.rs`, `corner_blend.rs`, and `adaptive_entry_pieces.rs`.\nRead the restart implementation history at c6b2d15e9.\nThe earlier claim was released. Searches found no duplicate PR or exact-file overlap.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll checks use the final source tree:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test adaptive_entry_pieces`: PASS, 6 tests.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: PASS, one touched-binary step.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\nSeparate temporary mutations prove sensitivity:\n- Disable blends in `pocket_emit.rs`: the new test fails with `no added planar corner blend arc at Z -4`.\n- Remove `with_solid_restart()`: the new test fails because the diagnostic is absent at (55.100, 5.000), Z -4.000.\n\nBoth mutations are restored. The final diff contains no production changes.\nThe pre-existing outside-channel test takes more than 60 seconds; it passes.\nThe new test completes below the displayed 0.01-second precision.\n\n## Not exercised and scope limits\n\nLight lane: Not run. The assigned test-only scope excludes release builds.\nThis conflicts with the general review policy that requests the light lane; no pass is claimed.\nNo app/catalog, GUI, full-workspace, heavy, release, or physical-machine checks run.\nThese software tests do not certify machine safety.\n\nEffort: low. No escalation.\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2341\n",
